  "notes": "The Mob's horror-showman, and the research gives one unusually precise compositional reference: \"melodic variations of John Carpenter's 'Halloween' melody\". That is a minor ostinato in a music-box/bell timbre, so `timbreHint` is `music_box_pluck`, `twoBarCellRepeat` and `loopVerbatim` are on, and `melody.colorTones` names the b6 and the raised 7th the research calls out — the leading-tone colour is what separates this from the parent's flat-7 minor. The density reading is deliberately split: `motifPitchCount` is 3–4 because the research says the note density is low, while `densityPerBar` reaches 8 because it also says the figure is rhythmically busy in 16ths. Two drum details are sourced rather than borrowed: the clap on 3 is doubled by a rim/snap on the preceding 16th, authored as a loud ghost at `2a` plus a `rim`/`snap` perc lane, and the hand-percussion and vinyl-noise layers are what `percs.gainOffsetDb` sits under. `bass808.slideIntervals` leads with `m2` because the research says short semitone slides — that is the one place this model's 808 differs from every other entry on this axis. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium: the tempo range is the inferred parameter, everything else traces to the album-level sonic description or a per-track credit. ⚠ The documented \"sub drops out entirely under chant hooks then returns on the downbeat\" has no engine field of its own; it is carried by `transitions.dropOutBeats` at 0.8, which is the nearest honest thing and is section-boundary rather than hook-wide.",
